LIS Test Case for "Add multiple irrigation scheme support in LIS"-- Github issue #107 with NoahMP4.0.1
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

This test-case performs a global 0.25 degree simulation with the
NoahMP 4.0.1 land surface model from 2000-01-01 through 2000-01-5 using
Princeton forcing data. This case demonstrates the concurrent irrigation 
without the new groundwater abstraction features. Test cases are equivalent to
the GLIrr simulation used in Rodell et al. 2026 JAMES paper.

This directory contains:

* this README file.
* it requres LIS to be compiled in multiple processor mode and the testcase used 120 processors for the global domain. See the job script run_lis.job.
* the lis.config file used for this test case.
* input directory with all input files that are needed to run this test case.
* TARGET_OUTPUT directory with LIS model output and log files by this test case.
* output_lsm.ctl GrADS description files for viewing the LSM output data.
* output_irr.ctl GrADS description files for viewing the irrigation output data.
* testcase_lsm.ctl GrADS description files for viewing the LSM output data in the TARGET_OUTPUT directory.
* testcase_irr.ctl GrADS description files for viewing the irrigation output data in the TARGET_OUTPUT directory.
